.env

# Real runtime data — settings.yaml (has a live provider config, not just an
# example), credentials, session/profile state, and the agent's own
# read-write scratch space. See docs/deepseek-harness/README.md.
#
# Everything under home/ EXCEPT .agent-presets/ — those are hand-authored
# content (the per-track team presets), not runtime data, and should be
# tracked. These files are already tracked from before this ignore rule
# existed, which is doing more work than the pattern itself: re-confirmed
# while adding the home-team*/ variant below that this `!` re-include does
# NOT actually un-ignore a genuinely untracked file at this depth — see that
# section's comment for the real mechanism.
deepseek-harness/home/*
!deepseek-harness/home/.agent-presets/
!deepseek-harness/home/.agent-presets/**
deepseek-harness/workspace/

# Same pattern, once per team (team0 = organizer testing, team1-5 = event
# teams) — see docker-compose.yml's deepseek-harness-teamN services and
# README's "Scaling to 5 teams" section for how these get seeded (copy
# home/settings.yaml + home/.agent-presets/ into each, once).
#
# CONFIRMED GOTCHA (the hard way, again): this `!` re-include only actually
# works for a path already tracked in git's index — `git check-ignore` (and
# a plain `git add`) still reports a genuinely untracked file under here as
# ignored, negation pattern notwithstanding. So a freshly-seeded team's
# .agent-presets/ needs `git add -f app/deepseek-harness/home-teamN/.agent-presets`
# once to actually get it tracked — after that, it behaves like any other
# tracked file (edits show up in `git status` normally, no more -f needed).
deepseek-harness/home-team*/*
!deepseek-harness/home-team*/.agent-presets/
!deepseek-harness/home-team*/.agent-presets/**
deepseek-harness/workspace-team*/

# Shared upload drop folder (app/deepseek-harness/upload-server/,
# docker-compose.yml's dsh-upload service) — participant-uploaded runtime
# data, not code; one shared directory across all teams by design, see
# docs/deepseek-harness/README.md.
deepseek-harness/uploads/

# Plaintext team passphrases, generated by scripts/generate-team-auth.sh —
# share these with teams out of band (slide/table tent), never commit them.
team-credentials.txt
